Package: pve-cloudprovision
Architecture: all
Depends: libjson-perl,
         liburi-perl,
         libpve-cluster-perl,
         libpve-common-perl (>= 9.0),
         libpve-storage-perl (>= 9.0),
         openssh-client,
         pve-manager (>= 9.0),
         pve-routedip (>= 1.1.2),
         pve-trafficd (>= 1.0.0),
         qemu-server (>= 9.0),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${perl:Depends},
Description: cloud server provisioning for Proxmox VE
 Creates virtual machines from the QEMU templates of the cluster with the
 CPU, memory, disks and any number of network devices chosen at creation.
 Each network device gets its own routed IPs (pve-routedip, any prefix
 length), rate limit, traffic quota (pve-trafficd) and guest IP config through
 cloud-init, derived from the routed IPs.
 .
 Servers can be reinstalled with a new template: the current settings are
 saved, the system disks are re-created from the template and the settings
 restored. Templates on local storage of other nodes are cloned there and
 migrated, servers can be migrated as usual.
 .
 Adds a "Create Cloud Server" button next to "Create VM", a Cloud Server page
 to the VM and Datacenter views and the /nodes/{node}/cloudprovision API.
